66:The source files also support drop-ins in the same way systemd does.
69:order. Top-level type drop-ins (\fBcontainer.d\fR) will also be included. If the unit contains dashes ("-")
70:in the name (\fBfoo-bar-baz.container\fR), then the drop-in directories generated by truncating the name after
72:further down the hierarchy override those further up (\fBfoo-bar-baz.container.d/10-override.conf\fR overrides
73:\fBfoo-bar-.container.d/10-override.conf\fR, which overrides \fBfoo-.service.d/10-override.conf\fR, which overrides
74:\fBcontainer.d/10-override.conf\fR). The format of these drop-in files is the same as the base file. This is useful
